      "message": "nit: I think this was already the case before but it doesn\u0027t seem like a good idea to do this math in `size_t` - if the number of bits in `ImmediateConstantMask` (which is `kMaxImmediateConstantsPerPipeline`) went over 32 I think it would silently break.\n```suggestion\n    // This bit math can be done in uint64_t because there are \u003c\u003d 64 bits in the mask.\n    static_assert(ImmediateConstantMask.size() \u003c\u003d 64);\n    uint64_t firstIndex \u003d byteOffset / kImmediateConstantElementByteSize;\n    uint64_t constantCount \u003d byteSize / kImmediateConstantElementByteSize;\n    uint64_t mask \u003d ((1u \u003c\u003c constantCount) - 1u) \u003c\u003c firstIndex;\n```",
